at="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUGIHARA, MASAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TORITANI, AKIHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MAKINO HIDEAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUMURA KOUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUGIHARA MASAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TORITANI AKIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAKINO, HIDEAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUMURA, KOUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUGIHARA, MASAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TORITANI, AKIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for producing a synthetic latex which comprises: introducing into a reactor a monomer and water in such a proportion that when the polymerization of the resultant composition is initiated at a given temperature and allowed to proceed adiabatically, the resultant maximum pressure inside the reactor is within the range of practical withstand pressures of the reactor; initiating the emulsion polymerization; and continuously or intermittently dropping the remainder of the water and monomer thereinto to carry out the polymerization. Thus, the temperature and pressure inside the reactor can be controlled so as to prevent a run-away reaction throughout the process and to stably conduct the emulsion polymerization. Productivity can hence be improved.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de production de latex synthétique, le procédé consistant: à introduire dans un réacteur un monomère et de l'eau dans une proportion telle que lorsque la polymérisation de la composition obtenue est initiée à une température donnée et s'effectue de manière adiabatique, la pression maximale obtenue à l'intérieur du réacteur se trouve dans la gamme des pressions de résistance pratiques du réacteur; à initier la polymérisation de l'émulsion; et à introduire de manière continue ou intermittente le reste d'eau et de monomère pour procéder à la polymérisation. Ainsi, on peut réguler la température et la pression à l'intérieur du réacteur de façon à empêcher une réaction d'emballement lors du procédé et à réaliser une polymérisation stable de l'émulsion, ce qui permet d'améliorer la productivité.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>